---
import Command from "./Command.astro";
import Stack from "./Stack.astro";
import Terminal from "./Terminal.astro";
import summary from "../samples/summary.ansi?raw";
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">A context profiler for coding agents</p>
    <h1>Your agent loads <em>26.0k tokens</em> before you type.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      System prompt, built-in tools, MCP servers, instruction files and skills are all in context
      before your first word. Quench reads the session history Claude Code, Codex and Pi already
      keep, and shows what each layer costs.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="#install">Install</a>
      <Command text="quench" />
    </div>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li class="mcp">Read-only</li>
      <li class="tools">Zero setup</li>
      <li class="system">Stays on your machine</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <figure class="diagram">
    <Stack />
    <figcaption>
      Fig. 1 — The first request of one demo session. Layers sized by characters; tokens from
      <code>quench runs --json</code>.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="hero-term">
    <p class="callout">Run it with no arguments</p>
    <Terminal title="~/code/acme-api" command="quench" output={summary} class="term-hero" />
  </div>
</section>
